[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64632,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Carcinoma of the uterine cervix, unclassifiable, is a malignant epithelial tumour of the cervix that cannot be further subclassified; diagnosis requires the exclusion of potential histological mimics, including primary and metastatic tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64633,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8020/3 Carcinoma, undifferentiated, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64634,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C77.Z Malignant neoplasms of cervix uteri, unspecified</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64635,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> undifferentiated carcinoma; poorly differentiated carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64636,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64637,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cervix</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64638,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical features are similar to those of cervical carcinoma in general. In a SEER analysis, the mean patient age was 42&nbsp;years (range: 32&ndash;58&nbsp;years), and 70% of cases were American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) stage&nbsp;I {17718897}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64639,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These account for a very small percentage of cervical carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64640,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "<p>Data are limited, but most cases are HPV-associated and/or block-type p16-positive {25884453}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-12T12:01:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64641,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>The pathogenesis is usually HPV-associated.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-12T12:02:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64642,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic appearance is similar to that of cervical carcinoma generally.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64643,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours demonstrate an epithelial phenotype but lack histological or immunohistochemical features of other specific subtypes of cervical carcinoma (e.g. squamous carcinoma, adenocarcinoma, and neuroendocrine carcinoma [NEC]). In some cases this may be a consequence of limited or non-representative tumour sampling. Diffuse p63 expression should elicit consideration of a poorly differentiated squamous carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64644,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64645,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64646,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> a primary malignant epithelial neoplasm lacking specific differentiating features; molecular analysis and/or p16 immunohistochemistry may help in determining HPV-associated etiology.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-12T12:02:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64647,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other cervical tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64648,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 313,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In a SEER analysis, the 10-year cause-specific survival rate was 84.9%, not statistically different from that of cervical squamous carcinoma {17718897}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:13:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]